# moon
.moon/cache
.moon/docker

# Elixir (poncho-style: one set of patterns here covers every Mix project
# added under the repo root, per-project mix.exs directories included —
# no per-app .gitignore duplication needed, see Stage 2 report).
_build/
deps/
*.ez
erl_crash.dump
.elixir_ls/

# Rust (pricing crate + pricing_native's native/pricingnative Rustler NIF
# crate, Stage 4). Build output for both actually lands under
# $HOME/.cache/baalbek-cargo-target/* (see pricing/moon.yml and
# pricing_native/moon.yml — a virtiofs workaround), but a plain `cargo
# test`/`cargo build` run without that env var falls back to an in-tree
# target/, so it's still ignored defensively. Cargo.lock is NOT ignored —
# committed for the same hermeticity reason core's mix.lock is committed.
target/

# Rustler copies the compiled NIF shared library here at build time
# (pricing_native/priv/native/pricingnative.so); it's a build artefact of
# native/pricingnative's source, not source itself. Unanchored (**/) since
# a mid-pattern slash otherwise anchors the match to the repo root, which
# would only match a nonexistent top-level priv/native/ and silently let
# the real nested pricing_native/priv/native/ path get committed.
**/priv/native/
